  <desc id="bdl01rejectionbeta-desc">Left panel: the Beta(2,2) density 6y(1 minus y) rises from 0 at y equals 0 to 1.5 at y equals 0.5 and falls back to 0 at y equals 1. The uniform proposal q(y) equals 1 lies below the peak, so q alone does not dominate the target, while the envelope c q(y) equals 1.5 touches the peak and lies above the density everywhere. Right panel: the acceptance probability k(y), which is 4y(1 minus y) for the Beta(2,2) target and 16 y squared (1 minus y) squared for a Beta(3,3) target with c equals 15/8. Both reach 1 at y equals 0.5; the Beta(3,3) curve is lower everywhere else.</desc>
